  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council, Monday 16 January 1911; 22 candidates for 15 seats. The Town Tenants' Association (formed to press the council to adopt the Housing of the Working Classes Acts) nominated eight, of whom six were returned. The other candidates carry no printed label; the Orange Society supported W. H. Wright, R. Courtney, W. J. Johnston, W. G. Hewitt, R. Anderson and F. W. White."
